a.common('Design a different minimal-data task','Justify necessary fields, access, shared output and responsible disposal for the stated purpose.',[(12,'W1 · Minimise the workshop-vote form','Remove unnecessary fields before collection rather than promising to ignore them.'),(13,'W2 · Challenge the anonymous-record claim','Explain how a key or photograph can preserve identifiability.'),(14,'W3 · Share the needed result with less exposure','Check the counts without publishing individual slips.'),(16,'W5 · Review an upload after your library plan','Use smaller fictional inputs or paper arithmetic and explain a first response to accidental sharing.')], 'For the fictional lunch-counting redesign, retain only menu choice for the stated purpose. Rice 9 + pasta 7 + soup 4 = 20. Name, birthday, address, photograph and favourite colour do not improve those totals. Model restricted handling by the teacher, sharing only the required totals, and disposal by an identified responsible person after agreed verification and activity closure under the approved process. The totals-only plan does not manage individual dietary safety: an authorised changed purpose requires a separately reviewed process. Do not collect real health or pupil data for this activity. Reserve Design a different minimal-data task for the independent first attempt.')
